        "h": "2. The INFORM Consumers Act: Surviving Amazon's Strict Business Verification",
        "body": "<p style=\"margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.75;\">Enacted to protect consumers from illicit goods, the US federal INFORM Consumers Act mandates that Amazon continuously verify high-volume third-party sellers (defined as generating 200 or more discrete sales and $5,000 or more in gross revenues in a 12-month period). Amazon must collect, verify, and publicly disclose four critical data points:</p>\n<ol style=\"margin: 16px 0; padding-left: 20px; list-style-type: decimal;\">\n  <li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><strong>Full Legal Company Name & Entity Type:</strong> Exactly matching the state Secretary of State database and IRS CP 575 notice.</li>\n  <li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><strong>Physical Commercial Business Address:</strong> Amazon verifies addresses by mailing a physical postcard containing a unique 6-digit alphanumeric PIN code. If your address is a fake virtual box or cannot receive physical letter mail, verification fails and payouts are permanently frozen.</li>\n  <li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><strong>Verified Business Telephone Number:</strong> Must receive automated verification SMS or phone calls in real time.</li>\n  <li style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><strong>Valid Bank Deposit Account Information:</strong> A US bank routing and account number issued in the company's legal name.</li>\n</ol>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.75;\">Under <a href=\"/usa-services/us-llc-formation/choose-state\" style=\"color: #06b6d4; text-decoration: underline;\">DigiFormation's Silver and Gold Packages</a>, non-resident sellers receive a verified commercial office address capable of receiving Amazon's physical verification postcard and forwarding the PIN code instantly via WhatsApp, guaranteeing 100% compliance with the INFORM Consumers Act.</p>"
