        "h": "3. Conquering the Amazon Tax Interview: Form W-8BEN-E Decoded",
        "body": "<p style=\"margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.75;\">One of the most intimidating hurdles for non-resident sellers is completing the mandatory Amazon Seller Central Tax Interview. Misunderstanding tax classifications can result in Amazon withholding <strong>30% of your gross sales revenues</strong> for federal tax backup withholding.</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.75;\">As a non-US citizen operating a foreign-owned single-member US LLC, your tax classification protocol follows these exact steps:</p>\n<ul style=\"margin: 16px 0; padding-left: 20px; list-style-type: disc;\">\n  <li style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><strong>Entity Classification:</strong> You select <em>Business</em>, then select <em>Disregarded Entity</em>. For US federal tax purposes, the IRS disregards the single-member LLC and looks through to the ultimate beneficial owner.</li>\n  <li style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><strong>Beneficial Owner Status:</strong> You identify the beneficial owner as a <em>Non-Resident Alien (Individual)</em>.</li>\n  <li style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><strong>Tax Form Generated:</strong> Amazon automatically generates an electronic <strong>Form W-8BEN</strong> (or W-8BEN-E). This certifies to the IRS that you are not a US tax resident and that your e-commerce profits do not constitute Effectively Connected Income (ECI) subject to 30% US backup withholding.</li>\n  <li style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><strong>TIN Input:</strong> You enter your company's 9-digit Federal Employer Identification Number (EIN) obtained via DigiFormation. You do NOT require an SSN.</li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.75;\">Once submitted, Amazon's automated IRS database validation verifies the match within 24 to 48 hours, displaying a green 'Validated' badge on your Seller Central dashboard.</p>"
