        "h": "11. Real-World Case Study: Pakistani Seller Scales to $80k/Month on Amazon US",
        "body": "<p style=\"margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.75;\">Consider the journey of Hamza, a textile entrepreneur from Faisalabad, Pakistan. Hamza manufactured premium home kitchen towels but struggled to sell internationally using a local sole proprietorship due to payment holds and high Amazon Currency Converter charges.</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.75;\">In January 2025, Hamza partnered with DigiFormation to establish a Wyoming LLC. DigiFormation provided his state Certificate of Formation, EIN, and commercial address. Hamza opened a Mercury Bank account, completed the Amazon tax interview in 10 minutes, and passed the INFORM Consumers Act postcard verification via DigiFormation's mail scanning portal.</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.75;\">By shipping inventory directly to US FBA centers and receiving bi-weekly ACH disbursements in USD, Hamza eliminated $2,400 per month in currency conversion losses. Today, his kitchen brand generates over $80,000 monthly on Amazon.com, completely managed from his office in Pakistan.</p>"
