        "body": "<p style=\"margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.75;\">Across digital marketing channels, aggressive formation platforms run ads declaring: <em>'Form Your US LLC for $0 + State Filing Fee!'</em> To an overseas entrepreneur operating on limited savings, a zero-dollar service fee sounds like an irresistible bargain. In reality, it is a classic customer-acquisition loss leader designed to ensnare non-resident founders into exorbitant recurring upsells, undisclosed compliance traps, and hidden statutory penalties.</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.75;\">When an inexperienced founder incorporates under a predatory platform, they quickly discover the hidden reality: the 'free' registered agent trial expires after 90 days, quietly renewing at $299 to $399 per year. The provider charges an additional $150 to mail a single PDF letter from the IRS. Worse yet, they fail to warn the client about mandatory state publication requirements (such as New York's Section 206 newspaper mandate costing upwards of $1,200) or annual minimum franchise taxes (such as California's non-negotiable $800 annual fee).</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.75;\">At DigiFormation, our philosophy is radical pricing transparency. We believe in providing an accurate, research-backed breakdown of the <strong>5-Year Total Cost of Ownership (TCO)</strong> across major states so you can forecast your startup cash flow accurately.</p>"
