        "h": "7. Step-by-Step Migration Blueprint: Moving from SaaS Lock-in to Self-Hosted Independence",
        "body": "<p style=\"margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.75;\">Transitioning your company from expensive recurring SaaS subscriptions to open-source software does not require an abrupt operational disruption. Follow this disciplined four-week migration pathway:</p>\n<div style=\"background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; margin: 20px 0;\">\n  <h4 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; color: #38bdf8;\">The 4-Week Sovereign Migration Schedule:</h4>\n  <ul style=\"margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; line-height: 1.8;\">\n    <li><strong>Week 1 (Lead Generation):</strong> Spin up DIGI LEAD HUNTER on your local machine or staging VPS. Test scraping a sample cohort of 1,000 niche prospects. Verify deliverability with the built-in MX validator. Once confirmed, cancel Apollo or ZoomInfo subscriptions.</li>\n    <li><strong>Week 2 (Audio & Creative Assets):</strong> Deploy DIGI VOICE STUDIO. Create synthetic voiceover benchmarks against your existing ElevenLabs audio files. Fine-tune speech pacing and inflection. Downscale your voiceover subscription to a free tier.</li>\n    <li><strong>Week 3 (Customer Engagement):</strong> Set up DIGI WHATSAPP SALES AGENT using your Meta Cloud API account credentials. Ingest product catalogs and FAQs into the knowledge store. Conduct live test conversations with staff before routing live customer traffic away from Wati or ManyChat.</li>\n    <li><strong>Week 4 (Office & Collaboration):</strong> Deploy DIGI OFFICE SUITE. Export Google Drive or OneDrive corporate archives and import them into your self-hosted instance. Test simultaneous collaborative document editing. Transition your team fully and terminate excess Google Workspace seats.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.75;\">Within 30 days, your company operates with zero software bloat, complete data ownership, and instant recurring cost reductions.</p>"
